00:22:05.857 --> 00:22:08.527
CANNOT SIMPLY PULL TO THE SIDE

00:22:08.593 --> 00:22:10.762
OF THE ROAD, AND IN AN EVENT

00:22:10.829 --> 00:22:13.665
THAT FORCES CREW TO ABANDON SHIP

00:22:13.732 --> 00:22:14.132
, CAN HAVE DISASTROUS

00:22:14.199 --> 00:22:17.169
CONSEQUENCES. AS A RESULT OF

00:22:17.235 --> 00:22:18.937
THESE SAFETY CONCERNS, THE U.S.

00:22:19.004 --> 00:22:20.806
COAST GUARD, THE MARITIME

00:22:20.872 --> 00:22:21.707
INDUSTRY, AND UNIONS

00:22:21.773 --> 00:22:23.909
REPRESENTING VESSEL WORKERS

00:22:23.975 --> 00:22:27.646
REQUESTED THAT CARB INCLUDE IN

00:22:27.713 --> 00:22:28.780
ITS REGULATIONS A BYPASS FEATURE

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:30.649
THAT WOULD ALLOW THE CAPTAIN TO

00:22:30.716 --> 00:22:34.419
TURN THE DPF OFF IN AN EMERGENCY

00:22:34.486 --> 00:22:35.587
. IF AN EMERGENCY WERE TO OCCUR,

00:22:35.654 --> 00:22:38.657
THIS WOULD ALLOW A VESSEL TO

00:22:38.724 --> 00:22:40.792
RESTORE FULL ENGINE POWER UNTIL

00:22:40.859 --> 00:22:41.860
THE EMERGENCY ENDS. WITHOUT THE

00:22:41.927 --> 00:22:44.496
SAFEGUARDS OF A BYPASS, A LOSS

00:22:44.563 --> 00:22:45.597
OF POWER COULD LEAD TO

00:22:45.664 --> 00:22:47.733
ENVIRONMENTAL DISASTERS. DAMAGE

00:22:47.799 --> 00:22:48.834
TO PORT INFRASTRUCTURE, AND VERY

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:51.770
SERIOUSLY ENDANGER LIVES.

00:22:51.837 --> 00:22:55.340
UNFORTUNATELY, DESPITE RECEIVING

00:22:55.407 --> 00:22:56.441
BROAD RANGING PUBLIC COMMENT IN

00:22:56.508 --> 00:22:58.944
SUPPORT OF A BYPASS SYSTEM, CARB

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:02.214
